<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<handout>
    <title>Disproving Injection and Surjection</title>

    <p>
        Let's start with disproving.
        Recall the following definitions.
    </p>

    <p>
        A function <m>f: A\to B</m> is <term>injective</term> if for all
        <m>a_1,a_2\in A</m>, if <m>f(a_1) = f(a_2)</m> then <m>a_1 = a_2</m>.
    </p>

    <p>
        A function <m>f: A\to B</m> is <term>surjective</term> if, for every
        <m>b\in B</m>, there exists some <m>a\in A</m> such that
        <m>f(a) = b</m>.
    </p>

    <activity>
        <task>
            <introduction>
                <p>
                    Disproving is like proving the negation.
                    Negate the definitions above to complete the sentences:
                </p>
            </introduction>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p workspace=".5in">
                        A function <m>f: A\to B</m> is
                        <term>not injective</term> if
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p workspace=".5in">
                        A function <m>f: A\to B</m> is
                        <term>not surjective</term> if
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
        </task>
    </activity>

    <activity>
        <task workspace="1in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Let <m>\mathcal{M}_{2,2} (\mathbb{R})</m> be the set of all
                    <m>2\times 2</m> matrices with real entries.
                    That is,
                    <md>
                        \mathcal{M}_{2,2}(\mathbb{R}) =\left\{ \begin{bmatrix} a \amp  b\\ c \amp  d\end{bmatrix}: a,b,c,d\in\mathbb{R}\right\}.
                    </md>
                    Prove that
                    <m>\det: \mathcal{M}_{2,2} (\mathbb{R})\to \mathbb{R}</m>
                    defined by
                    <m>\det\left(\begin{bmatrix} a \amp  b\\ c \amp  d\end{bmatrix}\right) = ad-bc</m>
                    is not an injection.
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

        <task workspace="1in" xml:id="ch08-task-surjdis">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Prove that <m>f: \mathbb{R} - \{1 \} \to \mathbb{R}</m>
                    defined by <m>f(x) = \frac{1}{1-x}</m> is not surjective.
                    <fn>Hint: Graph it! What's in the codomain but not in the range?</fn>
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>
    </activity>
</handout>